56-## 3. INDEX
57-
58-| Rule | Summary |
59-|------|---------|
60:| [Overengineering](.skilled/repo-rules/prevent-overengineering.md) | Build the smallest thing that solves the stated problem; take a costlier move only by naming what fails at the cheaper one. |
61:| [Scope discipline](.skilled/repo-rules/scope-discipline.md) | The requested scope is the deliverable. Adjacent problems get named, not fixed. |
62:| [Evidence and proof](.skilled/repo-rules/evidence-and-proof.md) | A claim is only as strong as the observation behind it, and a receipt confirms only what could have contradicted it. Distinguish observed from derived from inferred. |
63:| [Delegation and orchestration](.skilled/repo-rules/delegation-and-orchestration.md) | Delegating makes you the orchestrator; brief with evidence, and no single model's verdict closes a question. |
64:| [Blast radius](.skilled/repo-rules/blast-radius.md) | Size effort to what the change can break; no irreversible step without a named rollback and a yes. |
65:| [Root cause](.skilled/repo-rules/root-cause-and-debugging.md) | Fix the producer, not the symptom; every fix names the mechanism that caused the failure. |
66:| [Uncertainty and honesty](.skilled/repo-rules/uncertainty-and-honesty.md) | Never fabricate; mark the confidence you actually have and halt on a contradiction. |
67:| [Answer the actual request](.skilled/repo-rules/answer-the-actual-request.md) | Answer the request that was made. A warning nobody asked for, a quieter version of the ask, an invented constraint, a dressed-up refusal and a stall dressed as diligence are one failure. |
68:| [Communication](.skilled/repo-rules/communication.md) | Write so the reader can act after one pass: no table in a reply, nothing that does not carry information. |
69:| [Communication prose](.skilled/repo-rules/communication-prose.md) | How a sentence reads: sentence and paragraph shape, plain words, punctuation. |
70:| [Communication decisions](.skilled/repo-rules/communication-decisions.md) | When the reader has to decide or act on what you found, lead with the verdict, recommend one path, and say where you are going before a long stretch of work. |
71:| [Communication handoff](.skilled/repo-rules/communication-handoff.md) | End every turn by naming what is now the operator's to do, in the form that lets them do it. |
72:| [Hub routing](.skilled/repo-rules/skill-hub-routing.md) | A hub routes in two stages, so a mode registered on one surface is not reachable, and a gate run without its hub argument reports on a hub you did not touch. |
73-
74:Each file expands `AGENTS.md` and is bounded by it: where a rule file appears to
75:permit something `AGENTS.md` restricts, `AGENTS.md` wins and the rule file is wrong.
